# Unit09
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit09核心词汇

ignorant/ˈɪɡnərənt/无知的/He is ignorant of the basic rules.
ignore/ɪɡˈnɔːr/忽视/You shouldn't ignore the warning signs.
illustrate/ˈɪləstreɪt/说明/The teacher used a chart to illustrate the point.
image/ˈɪmɪdʒ/形象/The company is trying to improve its public image.
impact/ˈɪmpækt/影响/Climate change has a significant impact on agriculture.
implement/ˈɪmplɪment/实施/The government will implement the new policy.
implication/ˌɪmplɪˈkeɪʃn/含义/What are the implications of this decision?
implicit/ɪmˈplɪsɪt/含蓄的/There was an implicit agreement between them.
impose/ɪmˈpoʊz/强加/The government imposed a tax on luxury goods.
impress/ɪmˈpres/给…留下印象/Her performance impressed the judges.
impulse/ˈɪmpʌls/冲动/He bought the car on impulse.
incident/ˈɪnsɪdənt/事件/The police investigated the incident.
incline/ɪnˈklaɪn/倾斜；倾向/I am inclined to agree with you.
incorporate/ɪnˈkɔːrpəreɪt/包含/The new design incorporates several improvements.
incredible/ɪnˈkredəbl/难以置信的/The view from the top is incredible.
independent/ˌɪndɪˈpendənt/独立的/She is an independent and confident woman.
indicate/ˈɪndɪkeɪt/表明/The data indicates a clear trend.
individual/ˌɪndɪˈvɪdʒuəl/个人的/Each individual has different needs.
induce/ɪnˈduːs/引起；诱导/The medicine can induce drowsiness.
inevitable/ɪnˈevɪtəbl/不可避免的/Change is inevitable in life.
infant/ˈɪnfənt/婴儿/The infant is only three months old.
inflation/ɪnˈfleɪʃn/通货膨胀/Inflation has been rising steadily.
influence/ˈɪnfluəns/影响/Parents have a great influence on their children.
inform/ɪnˈfɔːrm/通知/Please inform me of any changes.
ingredient/ɪnˈɡriːdiənt/成分/Fresh ingredients make the food taste better.
inhabit/ɪnˈhæbɪt/居住/Many species inhabit this forest.
inherit/ɪnˈherɪt/继承/She inherited a large fortune from her father.
initial/ɪˈnɪʃl/最初的/His initial reaction was shock.
initiative/ɪˈnɪʃətɪv/倡议/The government launched a new initiative for education.
innocent/ˈɪnəsənt/无辜的/He was proved innocent of the crime.
innovation/ˌɪnəˈveɪʃn/创新/Innovation is the key to success.
input/ˈɪnpʊt/投入/We need more input from the team.
insert/ɪnˈsɜːrt/插入/Please insert your card into the machine.
insight/ˈɪnsaɪt/洞察力/She has great insight into human behavior.
inspect/ɪnˈspekt/检查/The officer inspected the building for safety.
inspire/ɪnˈspaɪər/激励/Her story inspired many young people.
install/ɪnˈstɔːl/安装/They installed a new air conditioner.
instance/ˈɪnstəns/实例/For instance, you can use this method.
institute/ˈɪnstɪtuːt/机构/He works at a research institute.
institution/ˌɪnstɪˈtuːʃn/制度；机构/Banks are important financial institutions.
instruct/ɪnˈstrʌkt/指示/The doctor instructed him to rest for a week.
instrument/ˈɪnstrəmənt/仪器/She plays several musical instruments.
insurance/ɪnˈʃʊrəns/保险/Health insurance is very important.
integral/ˈɪntɪɡrəl/必不可少的/Teamwork is integral to the success of the project.
integrate/ˈɪntɪɡreɪt/整合/We need to integrate technology into education.
intellectual/ˌɪntəˈlektʃuəl/知识分子的/He is an intellectual with wide interests.
intelligence/ɪnˈtelɪdʒəns/智力/Artificial intelligence is changing our lives.
intense/ɪnˈtens/强烈的/The competition is very intense.
intention/ɪnˈtenʃn/意图/He had no intention of leaving the company.
interact/ˌɪntərˈækt/互动/Children learn by interacting with each other.
